course: dictionary
lesson: 11224
title: The woodwind family
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An orchestra or band is split into families of instruments. The woodwind family is the group of instruments played by blowing, mostly with a reed or across a hole. Flute, recorder, clarinet, oboe, bassoon and saxophone are all woodwind.
explain: A family is decided by how the sound is made, not by what the instrument is made of. «The saxophone is made of brass but is a woodwind, because it makes its sound with a reed, like a clarinet.» The metal flute is also a woodwind, because you blow across an edge.
explain: Woodwind can also mean the players. «The woodwind section» is the group of players of these instruments in an orchestra or band. «Woodwind instruments» means the instruments themselves.
fact: Woodwind is a noun for the family of instruments, and also for the players in an orchestra or band.
fact: Woodwind instruments are played by blowing, mostly with a reed or across a hole.
fact: The flute, recorder, clarinet, oboe, bassoon and saxophone are woodwind instruments.
fact: Woodwind instruments were first made of wood, but some, like the flute and saxophone, are now metal.
fact: Woodwind is also an adjective, as in «woodwind instruments».
exercise: «The woodwind section played a soft, happy tune.» What is the woodwind section? | The seats at the front of the hall | The people who tune the piano | *The players of woodwind instruments in the band | The drums and cymbals at the back
exercise: Which of these is a woodwind instrument? | *Recorder | Drum | Trumpet | Violin
exercise: Why is the metal saxophone a woodwind? | *Because it makes its sound with a reed, not because of what it is made of | Because it is very quiet | Because it is played with the hands only | Because it is made of wood
test: How are woodwind instruments mostly played? | *By blowing, with a reed or across a hole | By hitting them | By shaking them | By plucking strings
test: «The flute is a woodwind because the player blows across an edge.» What is the reason? | *Because the sound is made by blowing across an edge | It belongs to the brass family | It is made of metal | It is shiny and silver
exam: Jordan says the saxophone must be brass because it is made of brass. Which is correct? | It is a string instrument | *It is a woodwind, because families depend on how the sound is made | It is a brass instrument because of its metal | It is a percussion instrument
